voc.txt was generated from a dump of the Albanian Wikipedia like so:

perl -CS scripts/wikipedia-dump-to-freq sqwiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2 10 latin1 > voc.freq
scripts/freq-to-voc 20 < voc.freq | grep -v "^'" > all.words
zcat web-sq-2026-11.tsv.gz | cut -f1 > keep.words
hunspell -d sq_AL -G < all.words >> keep.words
grep -Fxf keep.words all.words | grep '[aeiouyë]' > albanian/voc.txt

The dump used was dated 2026-11-01.

The first command extracts the article text from the dump and counts word
occurrences; freq-to-voc keeps only words which occur at least 20 times.
This is a frequency list, not article text: no sentence of any article can be
recovered from it.

Wikipedia articles quote many foreign names, titles and abbreviations, so a
word is then kept only if it is also known as Albanian, and has a vowel. It is
known if it is in the web lexicon web-sq-2026-11.tsv.gz of the albanian-stemmer
project (https://github.com/edisnord/albanian-stemmer, data/lexicons/; words
seen at least 5 times in Albanian web text), or if the Albanian Hunspell
dictionary (sq_AL, version 1.2 by Luan Kelmendi) accepts it. These only select
words: every word in voc.txt comes from the Wikipedia frequency list.

output.txt was generated from voc.txt by running it through the stemmer:

stemwords -l albanian -c UTF_8 -i albanian/voc.txt -o albanian/output.txt

